# Fixing Common OmniLib House System Problems

This guide helps library staff, support teams, and system admins quickly fix the most common technical issues on the OmniLib House platform.

---

## Quick Problem Finder (Diagnostic Matrix)

| What is happening? | Error Code | Why is it happening? | Where to look for logs |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Readers cannot swap a book face-to-face. | `ERR_DCTP_EXPIRED_TOKEN` | The 6-digit swap code was not entered within the 5-minute time limit. | `/var/log/omnilib/dctp_handshakes.log` |
| Internal chat rooms are down or messages are not sending. | `ERR_WS_BROKER_DISCONNECT` | The background chat server lost connection or timed out. | `/var/log/omnilib/websocket_chat.log` |
| Event videos or audiobooks will not load or keep buffering. | `ERR_CDN_URL_EXPIRED` | The temporary internet link for the video expired or broke. | `/var/log/omnilib/media_delivery.log` |
| A book returned in a different city does not show up in searches yet. | `ERR_ILLR_INDEX_LAG` | High system traffic delayed the automatic update between city branches. | `/var/log/omnilib/inventory_search.log` |

---

## Step-by-Step Fixes

### Fix 1: Solving Book Swap Timeouts (`ERR_DCTP_EXPIRED_TOKEN`)

This happens when phone network lag slows down a face-to-face book swap between two readers.

1. **Check if the code is still valid:** Type this command into the background terminal to see if the database still remembers the code:
   ```bash
   redis-cli GET token:asset_barcode_99011_omega
   ```
2. **Get a new code:** If the system returns empty (`nil`), the code has expired. Tell the book owner to hit refresh in the mobile app to get a brand-new 6-digit code.
3. **Forced Librarian Override:** If network issues keep blocking the phone transfer, a librarian can force the system to change the book owner by running this command:
   ```bash
   python system_utils.py --force-custody-transfer --asset="barcode_99011_omega" --recipient="usr_10442_beta"
   ```

---

### Fix 2: Solving Chat Room Outages (`ERR_WS_BROKER_DISCONNECT`)

This happens when a sudden rush of readers trying to coordinate book swaps overloads the messaging system.

1. **Find the dropouts:** Look at the last 100 lines of the chat log to see if the system is forcing users offline:
   ```bash
   tail -n 100 /var/log/omnilib/websocket_chat.log | grep -i "connection_terminated"
   ```
2. **Reset the chat system:** If widespread disconnections are visible, restart the chat broker software to clear out jammed connections and get messaging working again:
   ```bash
   sudo systemctl restart omnilib-chat-broker.service
   ```

---

### Fix 3: Solving Video Playback Failures (`ERR_CDN_URL_EXPIRED`)

This happens when users try to watch recorded author events or book signings from home and the video player fails to load.

1. **Make sure the file exists:** Check the cloud storage folder directly to ensure the original video file was not accidentally deleted:
   ```bash
   aws s3 ls s3://omnilib-media-vault/events/event_302_raw.mp4
   ```
2. **Refresh the video links:** If the file is safe but links keep breaking, run this media tool to refresh the streaming file segments:
   ```bash
   ffmpeg -i event_302_raw.mp4 -codec:v libx264 -codec:a aac -f hls -hls_time 10 -hls_playlist_type vod ./assets/streams/event_302.m3u8
   ```
